## Catalog types (three modes)

Enum:
- `src/Bible.Alarm.Shared/Models/Enums/CatalogType.cs`

### 1) Flat

- publications: most **vocal music**, **video**
- shape: Publication → Tracks
- API: **GETPUBMEDIALINKS only** (no mediator for track URLs). One request per pub/language: `pub={code}&fileformat=MP3|MP4&langwritten={lang}` (no `track=`). Response contains all tracks; track numbers come from JSON `track` field.

### 2) Sectioned

- publications: **Bible** (books/parts), **melody music** (e.g. `iam` discs/sections)
- shape: Publication → Sections → Tracks
- API: **GETPUBMEDIALINKS only**. One request per section: Bible-style `pub={publicationCode}&booknum={sectionCode}`; melody disc-style `pub={sectionCode}`. No `track=` param; response contains all tracks for that section.

### 3) MediatorSectioned

- publications: all in **JwSourceHelper.AllMediatorPublicationCodes**: **Dramas** (Dramas, DramaticBibleReadings, DramasGoodNews, VODMovies*), **Series** (VODLFFVideosAD, SeriesDigForTreasures, Series*, VODLovePeople, etc.), **Children**, **Broadcasting**, **Teenagers**, **Family**, **Programs and Events**, **Activities**, **Meetings and Ministry**, **Organization**, **Faith and Bible**, **Interviews and Experiences**.
- shape: **Mediator API only** for track CDN URLs. Single mediator response `GET /categories/{lang}/{categoryKey}` contains all tracks: `category.media[].files[].progressiveDownloadURL` is the CDN URL; `naturalKey` gives TrackCode (e.g. `pub-iaoh_E_12_AUDIO` → `iaoh-12`). Do **not** call GETPUBMEDIALINKS for mediator publications. When using GETPUBMEDIALINKS for other pubs we do not call mediator. **Track param is never passed** anywhere.

