## APIs used (and what for)

### GETPUBMEDIALINKS (primary)

Constant:
- `AppConstants.ApiEndpoints.JwOrgIndexServiceBaseUrl = "https://b.jw-cdn.org/apis/pub-media/GETPUBMEDIALINKS"`

Used for:
- Bible audio links
- vocal music links
- melody music links
- video links
- drama links (after section discovery)

Common query params (varies by catalog type):
- `output=json`
- `pub={publicationCode}`
- `fileformat=mp3|mp4`
- `langwritten={LanguageCode}` (e.g. `E`)
- `alllangs=1` during discovery
- section selection for sectioned publications:
  - Bible: `booknum={sectionCode}`
  - Melody discs (e.g. `iam-9`): `pub={sectionCode}` (disc code becomes the pub)

### Mediator API (category discovery)

Constants:
- `AppConstants.ApiEndpoints.JwOrgMediatorApiBaseUrl` – primary (app.jw-cdn.org)
- `AppConstants.ApiEndpoints.JwOrgMediatorApiBaseUrls` – `["https://b.jw-cdn.org/apis/mediator/v1", "https://app.jw-cdn.org/apis/mediator/v1"]` for random pick / retry

Use `GetPubMediaLinksRetry.GetStringAsync(httpClient, JwOrgMediatorApiBaseUrls, pathAndQuery)` (or cataloger `DownloadUtility.GetMediatorAsync(pathAndQuery)`) so requests try each base in random order.

Used mainly for:
- drama section discovery (and in some cases localized metadata)

### Languages list (seed language table)

Cataloger seeds the full language list using the JW site language endpoint:
- implemented in `.tools/Bible.Alarm.Cataloger/Seeders/LanguageSeeder.cs` (called from `DbSeeder`)

