## Sample API Links for Track CDN URLs

**Base URL**: `https://b.jw-cdn.org/apis/pub-media/GETPUBMEDIALINKS`

We **never pass `track=`**. Requests are at **publication** or **section** level; the API response contains all tracks (each with a `track` field in the JSON). LookUpPath / refetch URLs are built the same way.

### Bible Publications (bi12, nwt, osg, pksjj)

**Format** (section-level; no `track=`): `?output=json&pub={pubCode}&booknum={bookNumber}&fileformat=MP3&alllangs=0&langwritten={langCode}`

Examples:
- **nwt** Book 1 (all tracks): `?output=json&pub=nwt&booknum=1&fileformat=MP3&alllangs=0&langwritten=E`
- **bi12** Book 1 (all tracks): `?output=json&pub=bi12&booknum=1&fileformat=MP3&alllangs=0&langwritten=E`

**TrackCode Source**: `trackFile["track"]` from JSON response (e.g., `"1"`, `"2"`). Match track in response by track number.

### iam (Kingdom Melodies)

**Format** (section-level; no `track=`): `?output=json&pub={discCode}&fileformat=MP3&alllangs=0&langwritten=E`

Examples:
- Disc 1 (all tracks): `?output=json&pub=iam-1&fileformat=MP3&alllangs=0&langwritten=E`
- Disc 2 (all tracks): `?output=json&pub=iam-2&fileformat=MP3&alllangs=0&langwritten=E`

**TrackCode Source**: `trackFile["track"]` from JSON response (per disc). Match track in response by track number.

### Dramas (Mediator-discovered: Dramas, DramaticBibleReadings, VOD*, SeriesDigForTreasures, etc.)

**Mediator only**: Do **not** call GETPUBMEDIALINKS for mediator publications. All track CDN URLs come from the **mediator API** response: `GET /apis/mediator/v1/categories/{lang}/{categoryKey}`. Each track: `category.media[].files[].progressiveDownloadURL` is the CDN URL; `naturalKey` (e.g. `pub-iaoh_E_12_AUDIO`) yields TrackCode (e.g. `iaoh-12`). No per-track GETPUBMEDIALINKS requests.

### Music Publications (sjjc, sjji, snv)

**Format** (pub-level; no `track=`): `?output=json&pub={pubCode}&fileformat=MP3&alllangs=0&langwritten={langCode}`

Examples:
- **sjjc** (all tracks): `?output=json&pub=sjjc&fileformat=MP3&alllangs=0&langwritten=E`
- **sjji** (all tracks): `?output=json&pub=sjji&fileformat=MP3&alllangs=0&langwritten=E`
- **snv** (all tracks): `?output=json&pub=snv&fileformat=MP3&alllangs=0&langwritten=E`

**TrackCode Source**: `track` from JSON response. Match track in response by track number.

### Video Publications (DramasGoodNews)

**Mediator only**: Use Mediator API `GET /apis/mediator/v1/categories/{lang}/DramasGoodNews`. Same as other mediator publications; no GETPUBMEDIALINKS. Pub code = category key.

### Catalog validation (sample vs API)

After seeding, the cataloger runs **CatalogValidator** (`.tools/Bible.Alarm.Cataloger/Utility/CatalogValidator.cs`): it loads sample tracks from the DB (nwt, bi12, sjjc, osg, iam, DramasGoodNews, thv, Dramas, SeriesDigForTreasures, VODMoviesBibleTimes, etc.). For GETPUBMEDIALINKS publications it builds the URL at **section or publication level** (no `track=`) from **UrlParams**, fetches the API, and compares. For mediator publications validation may use mediator or stored CDN. It compares:
- **Publication name**: API `pubName` vs DB `BiblePublication.Name`. For **sectioned/mediator** publications the API often returns the **section or episode title** (e.g. "Genesis", "Kingdom Melodies, Volume 1", "JW Broadcasting") rather than the publication name; the validator treats title match as pass for these.
- **Track title**: API first track `title` vs DB `BiblePublicationTrack.Title`.

So a "pass" means the stored URL params and track title align with the live API; pubName differences for sectioned/mediator are expected and not treated as failure.

### Response Format

All endpoints return JSON:
```json
{
  "pubName": "Publication Name",
  "files": {
    "E": {
      "MP3": [
        {
          "file": {
            "url": "https://cdn.jwplayer.com/videos/...",
            "duration": 180
          },
          "track": 1,
          "title": "Track Title"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

**For Dramas** (no track property):
```json
{
  "pubName": "Drama Title",
  "files": {
    "E": {
      "MP3": [
        {
          "file": {
            "url": "https://cdn.jwplayer.com/videos/...",
            "duration": 3600
          },
          "title": "Drama Title"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

The CDN URL is in `files.{lang}.MP3[0].file.url` (or `MP4` for videos).

